__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
.env*.local
.venv/
.DS_Store
bakeoff_results.json
digests/
site/node_modules/
site/.next/
site/content/digests/
.claude/worktrees/
# a run's throwaway Playwright scripts. They are written fresh each run
# against whatever needs looking at, so none of them belong in the repo.
site/*.mjs
!site/next.config.mjs

# Local volume-test fixtures for the skills library UI (never committed).
# Convention: dummy skills for layout verification live at skills/fixture-*
skills/fixture-*/

# tools/read_paper.py caches fetched papers here, per workspace.
.cache/

# Captured emails are people's data. site/.gitignore already ignores this for
# the Next.js app, whose cwd is site/, and site/lib/waitlist.js honours a
# WAITLIST_FILE override that can land it anywhere. The root copy is here so a
# holding pen written from the repo root cannot be committed by accident.
.data/

# A run's scratch, written at the repository root. Three runs have committed
# scratch from here, and all three were obeying a rule: the shared-/tmp
# incident of 2026-10-18 told every seat to stop writing scratch under a fixed
# name in /tmp, and the nearest place that is not /tmp is the working
# directory, which is this checkout. `.prbody-exo.md` and `site-server.log` are
# tracked on main because of it, and five files of it reached a pull request on
# 2026-10-27. These are the names the runs actually used. Root-anchored on
# purpose: `docs/` holds real .txt artifacts and they are not scratch.
/.inbox.json
/.prbody-*.md
/.p*.txt
*.log
